    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response is an `OwnerDto`, generated from `openapi.yml` and populated by MapStruct's `OwnerMapper`. I added `initials` as a derived, read-only field following the same pattern already used for `displayName`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (so it appears on the generated `OwnerDto`).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `initials` mapping that delegates to a small `initials(owner)` default method, which composes a private `initial(name)` helper. The helper upper-cases each name's first letter and appends a dot, so `firstName=\"john\"`, `lastName=\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`. The helper handles null/empty names gracefully and is the single place that logic lives, kept alongside the sibling `displayName` derivation rather than bloating any class.\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` and the full suite both pass.",
